to a non-autonomous obstacle problem, formulated as
 \begin{equation*}
 \min\left \{ \mathcal{K}(u), \mathcal{I}_\psi(u,\omega), \mathcal{E}_\omega(u,\omega) \right \}, 
 \end{equation*}
 where the functionals $\mathcal{K}(u)$, $\mathcal{I}_\psi(u,\omega)$, and $\min \left \{ \mathcal{E}_\omega(u,\omega) \right \}$ represent the convex dual of the Dirichlet form, the indicator function of the set containing the obstacle problem with a time-dependent coefficient matrix $\omega$, and the convex dual of the Dirichlet form with a coefficient matrix $\omega$ that is equal to $\omega(t)$ for almost every time instance $t\in (-\infty,0)$ and equals an arbitrary positive definite matrix $ \omega(\infty)$ for the remaining times. By combining the results from the convex analysis and a covering argument, along with an application of the intrinsic Campanato space theory, we have derived enhanced regularity conditions for the obstacle problem.
